---
title: Shepards pie
source: https://theeburgerdude.com/vegan-shepherds-pie/
author: ThreeBurgerDude
tags: [main course]
cuisine: British
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 365 F. 

== Potatoes

Cut @potatoes{1.5 pounds} into equal sized chunks and place in a #large pot{} with @water{}. Add whole @garlic{3 cloves}. Bring to a boil and cook until the potatoes are tender, ~{15 minutes}.

Drain the potatoes and return them to the pot. Add @butter{1/2 cup}, @nutritional yeast{1 tbsp}, and @salt{} and @pepper{} to taste. Mash the potatoes until mostly smooth.

== Filling

Dice @carrots{2 cups}, @celery{2 cups}, @onion{2 cups}, and @garlic{4 cloves}.

In a #cast iron skillet{} heat @olive oil{} until shimmering. Add the diced vegetables and cook for ~{5 minutes}, stirring occasionally.

Add @butter{2 tbsp} and @flour{4 tbsp}. Cook for ~{2 minutes}.

Add @dried sage{2 tsp}, @dried thyme{1 tsp}, @tomato paste{2 tbsp}, and @soy sauce{1 tbsp}. Cook until fragrant, ~{1 minute}.

Add @lentils{2 cups} and @vegetable broth{1 cup}, or more as needed to cover everything. Cook on low for ~{10 minutes} until the lentils are nearly tender, stirring occasionally. Add water as needed to keep the mixture wet.

> The mixture can burn easily, so keep an eye on the bottom of the pan.

Once nearly tender, take off the heat and add @frozen peas{2 cups}.

== Assembly

Transfer the filling to a #baking dish{} and spread evenly. 

Top with the mashed potatoes and spread evenly. Use a fork to make a pattern on top of the potatoes for texture.

Cover and bake for ~{20 minutes}. 

Take off the top and broil until brown, ~{3 minutes}.

Take out of the oven and let it cool for ~{15 minutes} before serving.
